operation or mutation signature\\n\\nField projection:\\n  { id status assignee }     Select specific fields\\n  { overview }               Use a base preset (minimal, default, overview, full, progress, planning)\\n  { observability-task }     Use project observability presets (project, epic, story, task)\\n  (omitted)                  Defaults to { id name status }\\n\\nBatching:\\n  Separate multiple queries with semicolons; results preserve source order\\n\\nSpawn policy projection:\\n  Full project_config reports the effective spawn-policy-v2/v3 contract,\\n  authority, normalized provider and role-effective policy, and exact config\\n  provenance. V2 additionally reports its frozen compatibility snapshot and a\\n  copy-ready v3 migration object; this is read-only evidence and never edits\\n  task-board.config.json. Spawn-preflight returns only the selected role policy\\n  and its actionable migration warning.\\n\\nOutput format:\\n  --format json       Standard JSON (default)\\n  --format compact    Compact tabular output (~40% fewer tokens)\\n                      plan() switches to the super-compact planning shape:\\n                      flat waves of IDs, one-line critical path, id->status map\\n\\nExamples:\\n  task-board q 'schema()'\\n  task-board q 'get(TASK-260211-abc) { id status assignee }'\\n  task-board q 'activity(TASK-260211-abc, limit=25, order=descending, view=effective)'\\n  task-board q 'list(type=task, status=development) { overview }'\\n  task-board q 'count(type=task, status=done)'\\n  task-board q 'summary()'\\n  task-board q 'summary() { observability-project }'\\n  task-board q 'get(STORY-1) { observability-story }'\\n  task-board q 'models()'\\n  task-board q 'models(agent=claude)'\\n  task-board q 'project_config()'\\n  task-board q 'provider_limits()'\\n  task-board q 'project_config(view=spawn-preflight, role=developer, agent=codex)'\\n  task-board q 'schema(operation=project_config)'\\n  task-board q 'schema(mutation=set_status)'\\n  task-board q --format compact 'project_config(); models(agent=codex)'\\n  task-board q 'get(TASK-1) { status }; list(type=task) { id status }'\\n  task-board q --format compact 'list(type=task) { overview }'\\n  task-board q --format compact 'plan(EPIC-1, active=true)'\\n  task-board q 'plan(scope=[EPIC-1, STORY-2, TASK-3], mode=children)'\\n\\nUsage:\\n  task-board q <query> [flags]\\n\\nAliases:\\n  q, query\\n\\nFlags:\\n      --format string   Output format: \\\"json\\\" or \\\"compact\\\" (default \\\"json\\\")\\n  -h, --help            help for q\\n\\nGlobal Flags:\\n      --board-dir string         Path to the board directory (overrides TASK_BOARD_DIR and config local.board_dir) (default \\\".task-board\\\")\\n      --context-profile string   Agent context profile override: full or lite\\n      --insecure                 Skip TLS certificate verification (for self-signed certs)\\n      --json                     Output in JSON format\\n      --no-update-check          Disable automatic update check\\n      --remote string            Remote board server URL (overrides TASK_BOARD_REMOTE)\\n      --remote-board string      Remote board ID (overrides TASK_BOARD_ID)\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 4232,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 1058,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"bash","outcome":"success"}}}
